================================================================================================                             >>> SYMPHONY VIM QUICK GUIDE [V7] <<<                                                   NORMAL / INSERT / COMMAND       |       96 x 40 ASCII                      ================================================================================================ >>>[ GET STARTED ]<<<                          | >>>[ FILE / COMPILER ]<<<                      1. Press i to enter INSERT mode.               | :w       Save source to SSD                    2. Type your BASIC program.                    | :e       Reload saved source                   3. Press Esc to return to NORMAL.              | :c       Compile current source                4. Type :c then press Enter.                   | :r       Run compiled program                  5. Type :r then press Enter.                   | :wq      Save and quit                         6. Type :w then Enter to save.                 | :q       Quit (stops CPU)                                                                     |                                                >>>[ MODES ]<<<                                | >>>[ INSERT / APPEND (NORMAL) ]<<<             NORMAL   Navigate and edit                     | i          Insert at cursor                    INSERT   Type text                             | a          Insert after cursor                 COMMAND  Type : from NORMAL                    | I / A      Insert at line start / end          Esc      Return to NORMAL                      | o / O      New line below / above                                                             |                                                >>>[ MOVEMENT (NORMAL) ]<<<                    | >>>[ DELETE / UNDO (NORMAL) ]<<<               h / l      Left / Right                        | x          Delete current character            j / k      Down / Up                           | X          Backspace                           0 / $      Start / end of line                 | dd         Delete current line                 gg / G     Start / end of file                 | r + key    Replace one character               Arrow keys also supported                      | u          Undo (one level)                                                                   | Ctrl+R     Redo (one level)                                                                   |                                                >>>[ WHILE TYPING (INSERT) ]<<<                | >>>[ IMPORTANT TIPS ]<<<                       Enter       New line                           | Press Enter after : commands.                  Tab         Insert 4 spaces                    | Compile again after editing.                   Backspace   Delete previous char               | Output and errors appear in Terminal.          Delete      Delete next char                   | Changes saved ONLY with :w / :wq.              Shift/Caps  Type uppercase                     | SSD contents auto-load at startup.                                                            |                                                >>>[ FIRST TEST PROGRAM ]<<<                   | >>>[ WORKFLOW ]<<<                             LET A = 2                                      | i -> write code -> Esc                         PRINT A * 3                                    | :c -> wait for compile OK                      END                                            | :r -> see Terminal result: 6                                                                  | :w -> save to SSD                                                                             |                                                Symphony Vim is a small Vim-like subset.       | Physical Location keyboard required.          